{"query":"Property Price & Trends  official site amenities","follow_up_questions":null,"answer":null,"images":[],"results":[{"url":"https://www.casagrand.co.in/blog/property-in-bangalore-price-trends-and-future-of-the-real-estate-market","title":"Property Rates In Bangalore 2026 : Bangalore Property Prices & Trends","content":"Casagrand Vivacity (Electronic City)\n\nCasagrand Vivacity in Electronic City offers an integrated community with 2, 3, and 4 BHK apartments, including exclusive penthouses, spread over substantial open space. Amenities include a world-class clubhouse and premium aquatic facilities. Full-height French doors enhance natural light.\n\nA basement car park and vehicle-free zones prioritise safety. Located near major IT campuses, schools, hospitals, and retail centres, Vivacity blends Bangalore’s high-tech ecosystem with residential convenience.\n\n## Stay on top of the Real Estate Market in Bangalore with Casagrand [...] Casagrand Flamingo (HSR Layout)\n\nCasagrand Flamingo epitomises luxury living in HSR Layout, offering 3 BHK apartments amid 77% landscaped greens. Designed for abundant natural light and ventilation, it features a grand entrance and lavish driveway. Its prime location near top schools enhances its appeal, aligning perfectly with the Bangalore real estate future of premium lifestyle developments.\n\n Casagrand Amor (Akshaya Nagar)\n\nNestled in Akshaya Nagar, Casagrand Amor features meticulously crafted 3 BHK apartments with expansive podiums and landscaped open spaces. Boasting over 80 lifestyle amenities and 100% Vaastu compliance, its strategic location offers seamless access to top schools, hospitals, retail hubs, and IT campuses, embodying the Bangalore real estate future. [...] 1. Price Spectrum:The price trend data indicates a phase of consistent growth over five years, culminating in strong demand for residential property in Bangalore across both premium and emerging segments.\n2. Premium Localities:Established neighbourhoods such as Indiranagar, Koramangala, and Jayanagar continue to dominate with higher price valuations, supported by superior social infrastructure, education, and lifestyle amenities.\n3. Emerging Corridors:Areas including Electronic City, Sarjapur Road, and northern suburbs like Yelahanka have experienced accelerated appreciation driven by improved metro connectivity and growing employment hubs.","score":0.5005133,"raw_content":null,"id":"221ec8-00"},{"url":"https://www.magicbricks.com/Property-Rates-Trends","title":"Property Rates and Trends in India | Real Estate Prices in India City-Wise","content":"What factors influence property prices in a locality?\n\nProperty prices in a locality are usually influenced by multiple factors, like Location and connectivity, infrastructure development, demand and supply, quality of project and builder, and nearby amenities (schools, hospitals, malls, etc.,).\n\nCan I check property rates for my city or locality?\n\nYes, you can search property rates & trends for your city or locality on Magicbricks, and view detailed prices, trends, and historical data.\n\nCan I compare property prices across localities?\n\nYes, on Magicbricks you can compare multiple localities to check price differences and growth trends. [...] What are property rates and trends?\n\nProperty rates refer to the average price of specific city and locality, usually calculated by price per square feet. Property rate & trends data show how the prices have changed over time. It will help you understand market movement and investment potential.\n\nWhere does the property rate data come from?\n\nThe property rates & trends data is aggregated from active properties on Magicbricks. We also analyze the historical transaction records, and market research to provide a realistic property rates for the locality.\n\nHow frequently are these property rates updated?\n\nWe update property rates data once in a quarter to reflect the most recent market shifts.\n\nWhat factors influence property prices in a locality? [...] MB Research\n\n  Services & Tools\n\n  Localities & Projects\n\n  Blog\n Help\n\n  Help/Support\n\nHome\n\nProperty Rates & Trends\n\n# Explore Property Rate & Trends\n\nCompare prices, rental yields & growth trends\n\nResidential\n\nCommercial\n\nPopular Cities\n\n Property rates in\n\n  Ahmedabad\n Property rates in\n\n  Gurgaon\n Property rates in\n\n  Ghaziabad\n Property rates in\n\n  Kolkata\n Property rates in\n\n  Indore\n Property rates in\n\n  Mumbai\n Property rates in\n\n  Hyderabad\n Property rates in\n\n  Bangalore\n Property rates in\n\n  New-Delhi\n Property rates in\n\n  Chennai\n Property rates in\n\n  Jaipur\n Property rates in\n\n  Noida\n Property rates in\n\n  Pune\n\nFrequently Asked Questions\n\nWhat are property rates and trends?","score":0.39887524,"raw_content":null,"id":"ad153c-01"},{"url":"https://www.puravankara.com/real-estate-blog/top-real-estate-trends-modern-buyers-want","title":"Top Trends in Real Estate That Modern Buyers Want | Puravankara","content":"5. Health and Wellness Amenities Take Centre Stage\n\nAs health and wellness become increasingly important, real estate buyers prioritise properties that offer amenities to promote a healthy lifestyle. This trend has led to including features such as fitness centres, yoga studios, swimming pools, green spaces, and walking trails in residential developments. Buyers seek communities that provide physical activity, relaxation, and mental well-being opportunities. [...] ### How can I book a home with Puravankara?\n\nBooking a home with Puravankara is simple. You can explore residential projects on the official website, compare locations, floor plans, amenities, and pricing, and submit an enquiry for expert assistance. The sales team helps you understand project details, site visits, payment plans, and the booking process.\n\nCopyright 2026 | All Rights Reserved by Puravankara limited\n\ncall us\nENQUIRE NOW [...] Marina One’s 45+ modern amenities, including a 5-acre urban oasis and a 50m swimming pool, cater to the growing demand for health and wellness facilities. These amenities allow residents to lead a balanced lifestyle in their community’s comfort. Similarly, Purva Park Hill’s lush greenery and world-class amenities create a serene and health-focused living environment, making it an ideal choice for buyers who prioritise wellness.\n\n6. Luxury and Exclusivity in High Demand\n\nThe luxury real estate market continues to thrive, with many buyers seeking exclusive, high-end properties that offer a unique and opulent living experience. These buyers often look for homes with top-of-the-line finishes, amenities and a sense of prestige and exclusivity.","score":0.3254353,"raw_content":null,"id":"39eada-02"},{"url":"https://www.mahindralifespaces.com/blog/impact-location-and-amenities-on-property-value","title":"Location vs Amenities: What Impacts Property Value More?","content":"## Real Estate Trends in 2025: What’s Changing?\n\nAs the housing market matures, real estate trends in 2025 reflect not just homebuyer preferences, but also lifestyle shifts, infrastructure upgrades, and long-term urban planning. Homebuyers are more informed and focused on value, looking for homes that provide more than just a good location or size.\n\n### 1. Increasing demand for sustainable, well-connected homes is rising. - H3\n\nEnergy-efficient buildings and green certifications are now popular among homebuyers. People want homes that reflect their environmental values and lower costs. Easy access to public transport, like metro and rapid transit, also makes these homes more appealing.\n\n### 2. Smart, compact homes with shared amenities are preferred. - H3 [...] Location affects how much a property can increase in value. Being close to business centers, transportation, and services keeps demand high.\n On the other hand, amenities improve livability, drive rental interest, and influence resale decisions.\n\nFor instance, a home near a metro station (location advantage) that also offers co-working lounges and EV charging points (amenity advantage) becomes future-ready. It appeals to both end-users and investors seeking a home with convenience, community, and comfort.\n\nAt Mahindra Lifespaces, projects are developed with this balance in mind. The idea is not to choose between location and amenities, but to blend both into spaces that grow in value and elevate everyday living.\n\n## Real Estate Trends in 2025: What’s Changing? [...] A good home can provide a great location and helpful lifestyle features. We are setting the trend by building projects that offer great connectivity and enhanced living experiences.\n\n## Understanding Why Location Still Reigns Supreme\n\nDespite changing preferences and lifestyle upgrades, location remains one of the most important property price determinants for good reason. A home’s value is deeply tied to its surroundings, not just the walls within it.\n\nIn 2025, homebuyers continue to prioritize the best property locations that offer everyday convenience.","score":0.29335943,"raw_content":null,"id":"9b01df-03"},{"url":"https://trainingcred.com/blog/enhancing-property-value-through-amenities-a-strategic-guide-for-real-estate-professionals","title":"Enhancing Property Value through Amenities: A Strategic Guide for ...","content":"Properties with premium amenities see an average price increase of 10-25%. · Energy-efficient homes sell 20% faster than non-green properties.","score":0.2732414,"raw_content":null,"id":"ceff86-04"},{"url":"https://housing.com/price-trends/property-rates-for-buy-in-new_delhi_india-P6xfqdsey6cc3d95h","title":"Property Rates in New Delhi, India | Property Price & Trends in New Delhi, India - Housing.com","content":"Conscious about your budget? Some value for money investment options are also available in Bakkarwala, Tilangpur Kotla, Khera Khurd, Narela, Sector 95A where property prices are in the range of Rs 4419.00 - Rs 9440.00 per sq ft.\n\n### What are the best localities for luxury investment in New Delhi?\n\nIf you do not have budget constraints and aspire for a great lifestyle, Anand Niketan, Vasant Vihar, Hauz Khas, Greater Kailash, Panchsheel Park are remarkable locations with high-end projects priced between Rs 33200.00 - Rs 46481.00 per sq ft on an average.\n\n### Popular Projects in New Delhi [...] Popular localities for investment in New Delhi include Uttam Nagar where average prices stand at Rs 6972.00 per sq ft, Sector 24 Rohini where average prices stand at Rs 10194.00 per sq ft, Burari where average prices stand at Rs 5607.00 per sq ft, Paschim Vihar where average prices stand at Rs 19125.00 per sq ft, Dwarka Mor where average prices stand at Rs 7337.00 per sq ft.\n\nIf you are looking at investment hotspots that will yield good returns in the long run, you should consider Uttam Nagar, Dwarka, Sector 19 Dwarka, Vijay Vihar, Chhattarpur which are priced between Rs 6231.29 - Rs 17151.00 per sq ft.\n\n### What are the best localities for affordable investment in New Delhi? [...] ### Filter by Property Type in New Delhi\n\nHouse for sale in New Delhi\nApartments in New Delhi\nPlots for sale in New Delhi\nResale Flats in New Delhi\nBuilder Floor in New Delhi\nREA Group\nHousing.com\nGreat Places to work - Housing.com\nGreat Places to work in Asia - Housing.com\n\nHousing iOS App\nHousing Android App","score":0.23105894,"raw_content":null,"id":"977be6-05"},{"url":"https://www.eeshanya.com/blogs/how-amenities-impact-property-value-over-time","title":"The Real Impact of Amenities on Home Value Growth - Eeshanya","content":"Amenities play a major role in long-term property value by improving livability, increasing rental demand, and strengthening resale appeal.","score":0.22558756,"raw_content":null,"id":"8214be-06"},{"url":"https://www.globalpropertyguide.com/asia/india/price-history","title":"India's Residential Property Market Analysis 2026","content":"#### Table of Contents\n\n Property Prices and Price Index\n Property Demand Trends\n Property Supply Trends\n Rental Market: Rents and Rental Yields\n Mortgage Market and Interest Rates\n Economic and Social Factors\n\n## Property Prices and Price Index\n\nResidential property prices in India continued to rise in 2025, with the strongest momentum concentrated in premium segments and selected major cities. Preliminary data released by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) in February 2026 show that the All-India House Price Index increased by 3.58% year-on-year in Q3 2025-26, the quarter ending December 2025, while also rising by 1.24% quarter-on-quarter. At the city level, pricing remained firmer, particularly in the major metropolitan markets.\n\nIndia's house price annual change: [...] By contrast, demand in lower-ticket segments is likely to depend more heavily on government support and gradual improvements in affordability. In this regard, official releases on the government’s Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana–Urban 2.0 (PMAY-U 2.0) housing programme point to continued support for economically weaker, lower-income, and middle-income urban households, which should help underpin end-user demand over time. Knight Frank likewise expects affordable housing initiatives, easing financial conditions, and pro-business reforms to continue supporting buyer confidence.\n\n## Property Supply Trends\n\n### Launches Remain Elevated, with New Supply Increasingly Concentrated in Premium Housing [...] At the same time, PropTiger expects buyer behavior to become more selective, with pricing increasingly shaped by city-specific conditions, project quality, and micro-market fundamentals rather than broad-based speculative momentum. As a result, residential prices are expected to remain firm in 2026, but gains are likely to be more moderate and uneven, with developers in some segments relying more on incentives, flexible payment plans, and phased offerings than on further sharp headline price increases.\n\n## Property Demand Trends\n\n### Resilient Buyer Activity Persists as Demand Shifts Further Upmarket","score":0.22354692,"raw_content":null,"id":"2b8d96-07"}],"response_time":4.35,"request_id":"ea975bb3-2ed9-4f11-8d28-3731993528b0"}